From: lemezohaib <zhbkhan644@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 18:47:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] Disable lens dirty detection

With lens dirty detection enabled, the vendor camera HAL runs
MiAiCamera::DirtyCamera from libcamera_dirty.so on preview frames, which
reads past the end of the buffer on AOSP and crashes the camera provider
(SIGSEGV in DirtyCamera::GetResult) a few seconds into preview.

Report the feature as unsupported so MIUI Camera never enables the vendor
tag; this also hides the lens cleaning hint setting.

---
 smali_classes2/com/android/camera2/CameraCapabilities.smali | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/smali_classes2/com/android/camera2/CameraCapabilities.smali b/smali_classes2/com/android/camera2/CameraCapabilities.smali
index 92f5d4d..edee6b8 100644
--- a/smali_classes2/com/android/camera2/CameraCapabilities.smali
+++ b/smali_classes2/com/android/camera2/CameraCapabilities.smali
@@ -14773,6 +14773,11 @@
 .method public isSupportLensDirtyDetect()Z
     .locals 1
 
+    # libcamera_dirty.so in the vendor camera HAL crashes on our preview buffers
+    const/4 v0, 0x0
+
+    return v0
+
     .line 1
     sget-object v0, Lcom/android/camera2/vendortag/CameraCharacteristicsVendorTags;->SUPPORT_DIRTY_DETECT:Lcom/android/camera2/vendortag/VendorTag;
 
-- 
